Adds the L39 register check to qa/compose.py (not-so-supra-man, the canonical gate copy),
alongside the L34/D14 staging check the 2026-08-11 re-bless landed. Authored against
main@cf07a32. Claude does not edit gate scripts (Layer 8) — this diff is for the USER to
apply and re-bless at the next gate review (one review + one `integrity.py --rebless`
covers this and anything else queued):

    git apply docs/proposals/d15-expression-register-gate.diff
    # review `git diff qa/`, then re-bless per the Layer-8 protocol

What it enforces on every multi-character page job (see situation-expression-registers.md):
  HARD  panel_situation missing from the shotlist panel (2+ characters)
  HARD  staging register_pose / register_emotion missing, or outside the situation's register
  HARD  two characters sharing the same pose+emotion pair
  SOFT  >3 multi-character showcase/celebratory panels in the chapter (warn only)
Plus: the composed JSON body gains "dramatic_situation" when a legal situation is set
(mirrors the L34 "staging" directive injection it sits next to).

Example catch: a confrontation beat where a character carries register_emotion
"ecstatic-joy" refuses with — D15 (L39): register_emotion 'ecstatic-joy' for rook is
outside the 'confrontation' register. That leak (showcase emotions on non-showcase
beats) is the failure L39 exists to stop.

